      "In Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag, protocol stage 3.7 defines primary measures. Lock numerator, denominator, start and stop events, pause treatment, withdrawal handling, and censoring before calculation. Publish counts beside rates, medians beside ranges, and unresolved cases beside closed cases. This stage specifically evaluates valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases for contractor extension decision lag and retains its source reference, observer, exception status, and observation window for independent reconstruction.",
      "In Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag, protocol stage 3.8 defines quality controls. Check identifiers, timestamps, impossible sequences, duplicate records, missing destinations, and edits after observation. Automation finds inconsistencies but cannot make workforce judgments. This stage specifically evaluates valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases for contractor extension decision lag and retains its source reference, observer, exception status, and observation window for independent reconstruction.",
      "In Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag, protocol stage 3.9 defines sensitivity analysis. Repeat measures under reasonable alternate cutoffs, pause rules, and missing-evidence treatments. Exclude incident-triggered reviews separately and disclose when extreme cases drive a conclusion. This stage specifically evaluates valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases for contractor extension decision lag and retains its source reference, observer, exception status, and observation window for independent reconstruction.",
      "In Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag, protocol stage 3.10 defines privacy and security. Collect minimum necessary fields, restrict exports and identity crosswalks, log access, and define disposal dates before collection. Aggregate results so worker narratives cannot be reconstructed. This stage specifically evaluates valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases for contractor extension decision lag and retains its source reference, observer, exception status, and observation window for independent reconstruction.",
