      "In Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag, protocol stage 3.12 defines governance and stopping. Name protocol, data, operational, privacy, safety, and remediation owners. Pause on unauthorized disclosure, unsafe access, action without approval, corrupted sources, or loss of the promised boundary. This stage specifically evaluates valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases for contractor extension decision lag and retains its source reference, observer, exception status, and observation window for independent reconstruction.",
      "In Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag, protocol stage 3.13 defines operational interpretation. Convert findings into better evidence fields, recheck intervals, ownership maps, and testable exception routes rather than worker, vendor, or provider rankings. Verify changes with fresh cases. This stage specifically evaluates valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases for contractor extension decision lag and retains its source reference, observer, exception status, and observation window for independent reconstruction.",
      "In Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag, protocol stage 3.14 defines transparent reporting. Publish case flow, denominators, exclusions, unresolved cases, observation coverage, deviations, sensitivity results, and limitations together, keeping claims within the tested population, systems, and period. This stage specifically evaluates valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases for contractor extension decision lag and retains its source reference, observer, exception status, and observation window for independent reconstruction.",
      "Before analysis, pilot Analyze Contractor Extension Decision Lag on a small masked set and compare the event ledger with the frozen codebook. Reviewers should document whether valid requests, owner-ready evidence, decision time, access expiry, and censored cases can be derived without guessing, whether each included unit satisfies the boundary for contractor extension decision lag, and whether missing destination evidence changes the denominator. Revise the protocol before the observation window opens, then retain the pilot decisions as provenance rather than mixing them into the reported sample.",
